WEBVTT

00:01.180 --> 00:03.190
!!! REMEMBER TO ADD EDGEBLUR TO THE SUB TEXT, >>>>>>>>>NOT<<<<<<<<< THE LOGO/TS/OP/ED

00:06.190 --> 00:09.820
Beneath the glass ceiling of the <i>Galerie du Roy</i>,

00:10.190 --> 00:15.870
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.

00:16.620 --> 00:22.290
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival.

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
Ikoku Meiro
no Croisée

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
Paris. The end of the 19th century.
Beneath the glass ceiling of the Galerie du Roy,
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:38.720 --> 00:44.100
As I open the gate and step out into the street

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
asa no hikari ga mabushii

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
朝の光が眩しい

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
I can see the sun shining brightly

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
I can hear humming in the distance

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
kokoro hazumi tokete yuku

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
心弾み解けてゆく

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
It moves me and melts my heart

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
瞼閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
思い出す度に涙ひとつ

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
te wo hiroge hashiridase

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
手を広げ 走りだせ

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
Spread your arms out and take off

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
hi no ataru toori wo

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
陽の当たる 通りを

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
Down the streets where the lights shine

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
道行く人に 元気に挨拶

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
新しい 気持ちで深呼吸したら

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
この世界はほら いつでも 君のもの

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
And this world will always be yours

01:51.170 --> 02:01.010
Episode 02 :

01:51.170 --> 02:01.010
" Cheese "

02:15.150 --> 02:17.900
Good morning, Oscar-sama!

02:17.900 --> 02:20.070
Good morning, Yune.

02:22.280 --> 02:24.910
It's time for breakfast!

02:26.290 --> 02:27.160
Indeed.

02:51.650 --> 02:52.520
Um...

02:53.610 --> 02:56.690
May I help as well?

02:56.690 --> 02:58.860
Well, let's see...

03:02.160 --> 03:03.620
I'm already done.

03:10.330 --> 03:11.670
Wh-What's going on?

03:12.790 --> 03:15.380
It's no surprise that Yune is so sad.

03:15.380 --> 03:20.760
In Japan, people eat hot miso soup, rice, and fried fish for breakfast.

03:20.760 --> 03:23.510
It's a very daunting task.

03:23.510 --> 03:26.180
You have hot foods for breakfast?

03:26.180 --> 03:28.430
That's quite normal in Japan.

03:28.430 --> 03:30.020
Oh, I see.

03:30.850 --> 03:34.020
From now on, you're going to eat like French people do.

03:34.860 --> 03:36.190
Here, Yune.

03:36.770 --> 03:39.530
Thank you.

03:51.460 --> 03:52.420
What's wrong?

03:53.250 --> 03:54.420
Aren't you going to eat?

03:54.420 --> 03:55.380
Ah, yes.

03:57.040 --> 03:58.710
Itadakimasu.

03:58.710 --> 03:59.800
What was that?

03:59.800 --> 04:01.880
It's a Japanese custom.

04:01.880 --> 04:07.640
The Japanese put their hands together to give thanks to their food.

04:07.640 --> 04:08.640
Right, Yune?

04:09.010 --> 04:09.890
Yes!

04:15.810 --> 04:19.860
That's some bread left over from yesterday, so it might be a bit hard.

04:19.860 --> 04:22.700
It might be a little <i>too</i> hard for Yune.

04:36.880 --> 04:38.380
<i>Kamaboko</i>?

04:36.880 --> 04:38.380
TL Note: Kamaboko = Grounded fish cakes.

04:39.550 --> 04:40.920
It's cheese!

04:40.920 --> 04:41.960
Cheese?

04:41.960 --> 04:45.090
French people can't live without it.

04:47.050 --> 04:50.260
Is it that important?

04:52.390 --> 04:56.900
I had a pretty hard time in Japan
since I couldn't find any cheese.

04:56.900 --> 05:02.530
Japanese people somehow manage to live without any dairy products.

05:02.530 --> 05:05.950
Wait, wouldn't eating cheese be really strange for Yune, then?

05:06.570 --> 05:07.910
It's delicious!

05:07.910 --> 05:09.070
So you weren't crying?

05:09.070 --> 05:10.530
I wasn't crying!

05:11.540 --> 05:14.540
Can I have some of that, too, Oscar-sama?

05:15.160 --> 05:16.790
This is coffee.

05:18.250 --> 05:19.960
It smells very good.

05:23.010 --> 05:24.800
It'll definitely be too bitter for you.

05:24.800 --> 05:26.510
No! It's delicious!

05:26.510 --> 05:27.590
Don't push yourself.

05:27.590 --> 05:28.930
I'm not!

05:31.260 --> 05:32.720
It's delicious!

05:32.720 --> 05:34.680
If you say so.

05:52.660 --> 05:53.790
What are you doing?

05:54.250 --> 05:56.460
I'm taking these to my room.

05:57.830 --> 06:00.250
You can just throw it out if you don't want it.

06:00.250 --> 06:01.210
I can't do that.

06:01.210 --> 06:05.630
I'll eat everything that I'm served to show my appreciation.

06:05.630 --> 06:09.260
If I can't finish it all, then I'll save it for later.

06:16.020 --> 06:18.020
I don't understand this at all.

06:16.060 --> 06:16.140
Paris Illustrated: Japan

06:18.020 --> 06:21.770
You can't expect to understand it right away.

06:21.770 --> 06:30.700
I can't even comprehend why Yune would give away her mother's memento so eagerly.

06:31.200 --> 06:32.950
You didn't know either, did you?

06:32.950 --> 06:36.450
You had no idea that she could speak French.

06:36.450 --> 06:41.580
Well sure, but I knew that our feelings were being conveyed either way.

06:54.850 --> 06:58.350
It's hard to work if you're standing there.

06:58.350 --> 07:00.060
Oh! I'm sorry!

07:01.560 --> 07:04.980
I still feel uneasy with you watching me no matter how far away you are.

07:04.980 --> 07:06.400
What should I do, then?

07:07.190 --> 07:08.860
Have you finished cleaning?

07:08.860 --> 07:09.860
Yes.

07:10.150 --> 07:12.620
Why don't you go for a walk?

07:12.620 --> 07:16.450
I haven't gotten used to the <i>Galerie</i> yet.

07:16.450 --> 07:19.250
I'd cause you lots of trouble if I got lost.

07:20.370 --> 07:24.630
There are also some things I need to do around here.

07:26.590 --> 07:29.260
Go ahead and do them, then.

07:29.260 --> 07:30.130
Okay!

07:57.330 --> 07:58.410
Hey,

07:58.410 --> 08:02.210
when you said you had some things you need to do around here, did you mean watching me?

08:02.210 --> 08:04.290
What fun is there in that?

08:04.290 --> 08:06.960
Don't you have anything better to do?

08:06.960 --> 08:10.420
There are a lot of interesting things to do in the <i>Galerie</i>.

08:10.420 --> 08:13.590
You can go buy some candy if you want.

08:13.590 --> 08:14.720
I'm fine.

08:16.300 --> 08:19.060
You may be fine, but I'm not!

08:19.060 --> 08:24.730
I feel bad that you're standing around in this musty room full of metal shards and stuff.

08:25.650 --> 08:29.360
Am I causing you trouble by being here?

08:29.650 --> 08:31.190
Not exactly.

08:31.190 --> 08:36.410
You came all the way to France, so there should be plenty of things for you to do.

08:51.340 --> 08:53.380
We're going out.

08:53.380 --> 08:54.090
Come on.

08:54.090 --> 08:56.050
M-Me, too?

08:56.050 --> 08:57.720
But what about the store?

08:57.720 --> 09:00.850
That's what keys are for.

09:00.850 --> 09:03.060
What if a customer comes?

09:03.060 --> 09:06.150
If they really want something, then they'll come again later.

09:07.600 --> 09:08.770
Okay!

09:13.440 --> 09:16.860
There are many tall buildings!

09:16.860 --> 09:17.910
Yep.

09:22.330 --> 09:23.750
This is really popular!

09:23.750 --> 09:24.790
Really?

09:25.660 --> 09:26.330
Here you go.

09:26.330 --> 09:27.210
Thank you.

09:30.090 --> 09:32.050
Look, Claude-sama.

09:32.420 --> 09:34.470
It's a beautiful building.

09:34.470 --> 09:35.470
What is it?

09:36.680 --> 09:38.680
A <i>Grand Magasin</i>.

09:38.680 --> 09:40.100
"<i>Grand Magasin</i>"?

09:40.350 --> 09:46.690
They erected this monstrous building and claimed to have everything you'd ever need at a discount price,

09:46.690 --> 09:52.020
but they really just want to put the older stores out of business and create a monopoly.

09:53.400 --> 09:55.650
Is that so?

09:57.110 --> 10:00.410
Hey, Claude! Yune!

10:01.240 --> 10:02.620
Gramps?!

10:04.870 --> 10:08.000
The <i>Grand Magasin</i> is the <i>Galerie</i>'s enemy!

10:08.000 --> 10:09.330
Why were you-

10:09.330 --> 10:11.210
Don't be so stingy.

10:11.210 --> 10:13.750
Besides, it's good to know your enemy.

10:13.750 --> 10:17.420
You just bought some gloves for that girl or something, right?

10:17.420 --> 10:20.840
Hey, I just met her today!

10:20.840 --> 10:24.600
She said that she really wanted to visit the <i>Grand Magasin</i>, so I couldn't say-

10:24.600 --> 10:25.640
You could!

10:25.640 --> 10:29.600
Oh yeah, about Yune's kimono that was sold at the art gallery...

10:29.600 --> 10:30.940
Don't change the subject!

10:30.940 --> 10:34.650
Looks like the Blanche family bought it.

10:34.900 --> 10:35.900
What?!

10:36.940 --> 10:38.150
The Blanche family?

10:38.450 --> 10:42.830
Yes, the family that owns the <i>Grand Magasin.</i>

10:42.830 --> 10:47.120
They're nasty people who just buy everything in the area.

10:47.910 --> 10:51.580
They're the worst people to negotiate with!

10:54.750 --> 10:58.800
I can't keep a lady waiting.

10:58.800 --> 11:00.050
I should get going now.

11:01.050 --> 11:05.180
It's very nice of Claude to bring you out to town on his own.

11:07.390 --> 11:10.640
Sorry to keep you waiting!

11:10.640 --> 11:11.770
Let's go.

11:11.770 --> 11:12.690
Okay!

11:31.040 --> 11:32.210
Claude-sama?

11:34.080 --> 11:35.960
Are you worried about what we were talking about?

11:35.960 --> 11:39.670
Don't worry. A promise is a promise.

11:39.670 --> 11:42.550
I'll definitely get your kimono back.

11:42.550 --> 11:43.760
I need to.

11:47.010 --> 11:48.270
Okay!

11:55.270 --> 11:57.900
Paris' stomach. The <i>Marché</i> !

12:04.320 --> 12:07.080
We've got cheap, fresh apples!

12:07.080 --> 12:08.330
Take the whole box!

12:08.620 --> 12:11.790
She's very kind, but my kitchen is just too small.

12:11.790 --> 12:13.080
It's so tough!

12:13.080 --> 12:14.830
Don't slow us down.

12:14.830 --> 12:15.790
I know!

12:19.670 --> 12:22.260
What are these, Claude-sama?

12:22.590 --> 12:24.010
Artichokes.

12:24.010 --> 12:26.470
They're delicious if you boil and salt them.

12:27.100 --> 12:29.560
Artichokes... Artichokes...

12:29.560 --> 12:31.480
What are these?

12:31.480 --> 12:33.020
Mushrooms.

12:33.020 --> 12:34.730
They're good if you sauté them.

12:35.520 --> 12:37.940
Mushrooms... Mushrooms...

12:38.190 --> 12:39.360
What are these?

12:39.360 --> 12:40.230
Raisins.

12:40.230 --> 12:41.190
These?

12:41.190 --> 12:42.150
Tomatoes.

12:42.150 --> 12:43.240
These?

12:43.240 --> 12:44.240
Onions.

12:44.860 --> 12:46.740
Th-This...?

12:46.740 --> 12:47.990
Uh...

12:50.200 --> 12:51.620
I'll take the bacon.

12:51.620 --> 12:52.200
All right.

12:53.000 --> 12:54.790
Bacon... Bacon...

12:57.710 --> 12:59.460
12 centimes.

13:02.510 --> 13:05.510
Sorry, I'll just take half.

13:05.510 --> 13:07.390
Here you go. Half.

13:34.540 --> 13:36.670
The <i>Marché</i> is very fun!

13:38.420 --> 13:39.920
What's that?

13:43.210 --> 13:44.670
Claude-sama!

13:44.670 --> 13:47.510
Don't run. You might fall.

13:47.510 --> 13:48.840
R-Right.

13:48.840 --> 13:52.350
There are some interesting things over there, too!

13:52.350 --> 13:54.140
Hey, Yune!

14:26.050 --> 14:27.510
Do you want to look?

14:27.510 --> 14:30.220
They sell art supplies and paper.

14:30.640 --> 14:32.550
Paper?

14:33.010 --> 14:34.930
15 centimes.

14:35.890 --> 14:37.850
No, I'm fine!

14:54.410 --> 14:56.080
Hey, Yune,

14:56.410 --> 15:00.580
I still have some work to do, so could you peel the vegetables?

15:02.630 --> 15:03.670
Yes!

15:39.080 --> 15:41.330
I'm almost done!

15:53.260 --> 15:55.260
Needs more salt.

15:55.260 --> 15:56.760
Salt!

16:01.560 --> 16:02.560
Here!

16:06.270 --> 16:08.020
There we go. Perfect!

16:11.150 --> 16:13.410
This smell...

16:13.410 --> 16:15.700
Is today's dinner pot-au-feu?

16:13.410 --> 16:15.700
Note: Pot-au-feu is a French beef stew.
It's called the same thing in English, though.

16:15.700 --> 16:17.950
Weren't you going to eat out?

16:18.120 --> 16:23.080
It isn't gentlemanly to take a girl out to dinner the same day we met.

16:25.040 --> 16:26.790
You were dumped, right?

16:26.790 --> 16:28.590
Were you?!

16:33.430 --> 16:34.760
Here.

16:34.760 --> 16:36.680
Thank you very much.

16:36.970 --> 16:40.180
Then, uh...

16:42.890 --> 16:44.390
Itadakimasu.

16:55.110 --> 17:00.450
That's right. Japanese people don't use spoons for miso soup.

17:00.910 --> 17:02.290
Spoons?

17:05.370 --> 17:09.420
Look, You use it like this.

17:09.420 --> 17:10.340
Yes.

17:11.130 --> 17:12.670
Like this...

17:14.880 --> 17:15.930
Like...

17:17.840 --> 17:20.930
It's fine if you don't use the spoon.

17:20.930 --> 17:23.430
You can eat it how you usually do.

17:23.640 --> 17:25.480
No, I'm fine!

17:32.070 --> 17:36.320
That one's pretty stubborn.

17:54.550 --> 17:56.420
Good morning.

17:56.420 --> 17:59.680
Dawn is coming earlier nowadays, isn't it?

17:59.680 --> 18:02.430
Things are going to get busier.

18:03.350 --> 18:06.430
Claude, could you get bread for breakfast?

18:06.430 --> 18:08.440
I-I'll go!

18:08.440 --> 18:09.350
But-

18:09.350 --> 18:11.560
You won't know what to do.

18:11.560 --> 18:12.860
Want to go together?

18:12.860 --> 18:13.690
Yes!

18:15.610 --> 18:18.780
The bakery is at the <i>Galerie</i>'s entrance.

18:18.780 --> 18:22.450
You should be able to do the shopping as long as you know where to go.

18:22.450 --> 18:23.370
Indeed.

18:33.090 --> 18:34.500
Two and a half.

18:34.500 --> 18:35.670
Right away.

18:38.680 --> 18:40.220
They're so warm!

18:40.840 --> 18:42.300
They smell so good!

18:42.300 --> 18:43.390
They're delicious.

18:43.390 --> 18:44.350
Want a bite?

18:44.350 --> 18:45.970
Huh? Right now?

18:45.970 --> 18:47.100
Sure.

18:52.560 --> 18:54.900
It's fresh from the oven.

18:54.900 --> 18:56.740
Have a bite.

18:56.740 --> 18:57.570
Here.

18:58.780 --> 18:59.860
O-Okay.

19:05.620 --> 19:07.620
You may be able to hide it when you don't like something,

19:07.620 --> 19:10.170
but it's pretty obvious that you enjoyed that.

19:13.710 --> 19:15.960
Coffee, right?

19:16.210 --> 19:17.920
I'll save this for later.

19:17.920 --> 19:19.550
Just have a sip.

19:25.470 --> 19:26.390
It's sweet.

19:26.390 --> 19:29.390
I put lots of sugar in it.

19:29.390 --> 19:32.150
It's a type of coffee called Café au Lait.

19:33.520 --> 19:36.400
You really <i>are</i> a magician, Oscar-sama!

19:36.400 --> 19:37.860
You think so?

19:37.860 --> 19:42.490
I don't think I'd be able to make you like the cheese, though.

19:42.490 --> 19:44.820
Oh, no! Cheese is very good!

19:44.820 --> 19:46.870
You shouldn't lie. You can't eat it, right?

19:46.870 --> 19:49.410
I'm not lying! I want to eat it!

19:50.750 --> 19:53.170
How can you be so stubborn?

19:53.170 --> 19:55.710
You'll get too stressed if you keep pushing yourself.

19:56.090 --> 20:00.630
You keep trying to do difficult things, like using a spoon.

20:00.630 --> 20:03.300
You can take off your geta once in a while, you know.

20:00.630 --> 20:03.300
TL Note: Geta are the sandals Yune is wearing, and kind of look like clogs + flip flops.

20:03.300 --> 20:05.140
You're free to do what you want.

20:05.140 --> 20:08.560
If you don't like cheese, then just tell us!

20:09.020 --> 20:11.100
I like it!

20:11.100 --> 20:14.270
I want to enjoy it, too!

20:14.270 --> 20:15.810
What do you mean?

20:17.610 --> 20:20.900
You both seem to enjoy it very much,

20:20.900 --> 20:25.320
so I want to learn to like it.

20:25.700 --> 20:28.870
It's fine if you take your time to get used to it.

20:28.870 --> 20:39.800
But if I do, then I won't be able to make food that you two like!

20:53.180 --> 20:54.600
It's fine.

20:56.060 --> 21:00.190
There's no need to rush so much.

21:20.920 --> 21:27.510
aa marude yume wo miteru you na

21:20.920 --> 21:27.510
ああ、まるで夢を見てるような

21:20.920 --> 21:27.510
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

21:27.510 --> 21:33.310
yawarakana hikari no naka de

21:27.510 --> 21:33.310
柔らかな光の中で

21:27.510 --> 21:33.310
As I lie here in this tender light

21:33.310 --> 21:44.320
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

21:33.310 --> 21:44.320
目を閉じて耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

21:33.310 --> 21:44.320
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

21:46.150 --> 21:59.210
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

21:46.150 --> 21:59.210
あたたかく私を呼ぶ優しいその声が

21:46.150 --> 21:59.210
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

22:01.790 --> 22:08.380
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

22:01.790 --> 22:08.380
溢れる思いを伝えたい　この手から

22:01.790 --> 22:08.380
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

22:08.380 --> 22:14.680
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

22:08.380 --> 22:14.680
言葉じゃなくて　心で繋がる

22:08.380 --> 22:14.680
We connect through our hearts, not our words

22:14.680 --> 22:21.360
hajimeyou koko kara sodateyou nukumori wo

22:14.680 --> 22:21.360
始めよう　ここから育てよう　温もりを

22:14.680 --> 22:21.360
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

22:21.360 --> 22:27.820
atarashii hibi ga watashi wo matteru

22:21.360 --> 22:27.820
新しい日々が私を待ってる

22:21.360 --> 22:27.820
A new day is waiting for me

22:27.820 --> 22:41.540
mamoru mono wa kitto koko ni aru no

22:27.820 --> 22:41.540
守るものはきっとここにあるの

22:27.820 --> 22:41.540
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

22:57.060 --> 22:59.350
Oh, umeboshi?

22:57.060 --> 22:59.350
TL Note: Umeboshi are pickled plums.

22:59.350 --> 23:01.190
I ate a lot of those in Japan.

23:01.650 --> 23:03.690
Have some, Oscar-sama!

23:10.280 --> 23:13.160
It's a strange but surprisingly addicting taste!

23:13.160 --> 23:14.120
Yes!

23:14.530 --> 23:15.990
What's this?

23:35.260 --> 23:43.100
Episode 03 :

23:35.260 --> 23:36.010
Next episode:

23:36.010 --> 23:37.770
"Japanese Labyrinth".

23:37.770 --> 23:39.230
Please watch it!
